meta {
  name: Monthly expenses
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/reports/monthly-expenses?from={{sixMonthsAgo}}&to={{thisMonth}}&currency=CAD
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  from: {{sixMonthsAgo}}
  to: {{thisMonth}}
  currency: CAD
  ~accountId: acc_chequing
  ~projectId: proj_remodel
  ~includePending: true
  ~includeTransfers: false
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  User story 3. Expenses by category, month by month, with budget comparison.
  `from`/`to` are `YYYY-MM` and inclusive; default is the last 6 months.
  
  - Classification follows **the sign of the amount, not the category's kind** —
    a refund is an inflow even under an expense category, which is why every row
    carries `inflow`, `outflow` and `net`. Gross vs. net is the client's call.
  - Uncategorised spend is a row with `categoryId: null` and name
    "Uncategorised", not a separate bucket — one representation to render.
  - `monthlyBudget` is the category's setting; `budget` is that setting scaled to
    the period, so in `totals.byCategory` it is `monthlyBudget × monthCount`.
  - Child categories report as themselves and carry `parentId`; rolling up to
    parents is left to the client on purpose.
  - Two exclusions are applied by default and always reported back under
    `excluded`: transfer legs (`includeTransfers=true` to keep them) and other
    currencies (there are no exchange rates in this API).
}
